LAMMPS (4 Jul 2026 - Development - patch_4Jul2026-542-g4e5eb25ab6-modified)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# TIP4P-FQ liquid, FAITHFUL-RICK structure: lr_ewald=1 (INTRA-Slater + BARE-inter, his exact
# electrostatics per mdtpn.f) — the mu-gap root cause was lr_ewald=2's all-pair shielding.
# PREDICTION: mu -> ~2.63 (Rick 2.637). Stability rides XL (Rick's own stability = EL adiabaticity).
# Base: TRUE SLATER-OVERLAP kernel deck (`shield slater`): Rick's raw zetas,
# NO refit. Target: close the gauss-kernel port's -4% mu (2.53 vs Rick 2.637) — the deviation was
# the intermolecular J at intermediate r, exactly what the exact kernel fixes.
# Derived from in.tip4pfq_xl (KERNEL-REFIT gauss port); 256-molecule box built from Rick's own equilibrated
# mdtpn.dat config (build_box.py), vol=7660.31 A^3, rho=1.0 g/cc, fixed (NVT).
# Kernel: gaussian/pqeq erf(a_ij r)/r, fit EXACTLY to Rick's jrab() J_HH(1.5139)
# and J_OH(r_MH=0.8735) (see fit_j.py) -- the physically-operative rigid-body
# distances. Single `run` command (multi-run is a known samQEq calibration
# artifact); tail-window ave/time blocks report thermalized averages.
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       tip4pfq_liquid.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (19.712825 19.712825 19.712825)
